WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.747
AI writes code faster than ever.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.858
According to DORA 2025 and 2026,

00:00:05.858 --> 00:00:07.900
it speeds up delivery,

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.600
but also increases instability.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.895
Kaizen turns Claude Code into a

00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:14.729
controlled development cycle.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.319
Everything starts from a

00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:18.208
constitution: your principles,

00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:20.111
each with a verifiable check.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.730
The brainstorm defines
what to build.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.098
The plan decides how.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.536
Requirements, tests,

00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:30.702
rollback: everything is traced,

00:00:30.702 --> 00:00:33.119
then reviewed by
specialized agents.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.828
During the work, a
quality gate blocks the

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:39.979
end of a step while
tests are red.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.635
Reviewers chosen for
the changed code

00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:45.316
inspect it, and without their

00:00:45.316 --> 00:00:47.069
review, nothing is pushed.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.256
The PR is described,
its size checked,

00:00:51.256 --> 00:00:53.662
then it is followed
until it is ready.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.295
Merging and going to

00:00:58.295 --> 00:01:00.036
production stay in your hands.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.431
Finally, durable
lessons are captured,

00:01:03.431 --> 00:01:05.433
and read back by the next cycle.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.514
The goal: every unit of work

00:01:09.514 --> 00:01:11.241
makes the next one easier.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.747
Kaizen.

00:01:14.747 --> 00:01:15.912
For Claude Code.
